WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:02.580
Harry: From Croissant
Stuffers to festive pizzas

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.863
to gingerbread lattes,
we wanted to find out

00:00:04.863 --> 00:00:06.530
all of the fast-food Christmas menu items

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:09.050
in the UK, Japan, and the US.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.717
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.900
Here in the UK, we have
several festive drink options

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.620
at Starbucks, all of which are hot.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.453
We'll start with this one,

00:00:19.453 --> 00:00:21.570
which is the very festive
gingerbread latte.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.206
I'll do a Joe and try
and sip all of these.

00:00:24.829 --> 00:00:25.850
Actually not bad.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:26.683
Next up, we have this one,

00:00:26.683 --> 00:00:28.500
which is a caramel waffle latte.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.333
Then we have this one,

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:31.250
which is a fudge brownie hot chocolate.

00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:34.812
Oh.

00:00:34.812 --> 00:00:36.510
Ooh, I don't like that. That's bad.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.980
We also have this one,
which is a toffee nut latte.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.000
Are toffee or nuts
particularly Christmassy?

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.250
I'm not really convinced.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.950
It's very nutty. That is nutty.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:47.830
Then finally we have this one,

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.900
which is a venti eggnog latte.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.160
I think the last time I tried eggnog

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.530
was actually our last Christmas special,

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:53.560
and I haven't touched it since.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:54.880
I've kind of forgotten
everything about it.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:55.872
I'll try it again.

00:01:00.904 --> 00:01:02.245
No. What?

00:01:02.245 --> 00:01:03.253
This isn't a British thing.

00:01:03.253 --> 00:01:05.160
Do people in America
actually drink eggnog?

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.740
If you want to get your
Starbucks fix at home,

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.670
then UK Starbucks also offer beans.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.514
These come in the form
of a Christmas roast

00:01:10.514 --> 00:01:12.430
and also a blond Christmas roast.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:15.750
So, we have lots of delicious
Starbucks holiday drinks,

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.043
such as gingerbread latte.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.480
This is perfect for winter season.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.480
It warms me up.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.613
Not only my body, but also my heart.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:31.360
You should definitely try this.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.610
Next one: toasted white
chocolate Frappuccino.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:38.285
Hm.

00:01:38.285 --> 00:01:41.351
It's a little bit sweet,
but I'd say it's very good.

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:43.610
Every Santa Claus would love this.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.940
We've got toasted white chocolate mocha.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.012
Itadakimasu!

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.670
I'd say it's totally the same as this one,

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.680
but that means it's very good.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:55.522
And last one,

00:01:55.522 --> 00:01:57.988
we've got crème brûlée latte.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:04.786
Ooh, it's too sweet!

00:02:04.786 --> 00:02:07.011
It's too sweet!

00:02:07.011 --> 00:02:10.548
We also have the three
whole-coffee-bean options.

00:02:10.548 --> 00:02:13.210
We've got Christmas blend

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:16.218
and Christmas blond roast

00:02:16.218 --> 00:02:19.040
and Christmas espresso roast.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.060
Take a look at this.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.367
It says, "Christmas" ...

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:23.768
blah, blah, blah.

00:02:23.768 --> 00:02:25.550
But it's not Christmassy at all.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:28.780
Starbucks, you should
make it more Christmassy,

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.835
just like this.

00:02:30.835 --> 00:02:31.859
This.

00:02:31.859 --> 00:02:33.420
This is so perfect.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.770
And in the US, our
holiday Starbucks drinks

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:39.128
include all of these.

00:02:39.128 --> 00:02:40.850
You know what we doing.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:44.870
First one, of course, is the
venti crème brûlée latte.

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:46.078
I like crème brûlée.

00:02:46.078 --> 00:02:47.261
Let's make it a latte.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.630
Yeah, that's very good.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.486
Toasted white chocolate mocha.

00:02:54.569 --> 00:02:55.694
Holy s---.

00:02:55.694 --> 00:02:58.270
That might be the best one.
That's the one to beat.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.515
Irish cream cold brew.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.262
Whoa, first miss. Mm-mm.

00:03:04.262 --> 00:03:05.353
All right, next one.

00:03:05.353 --> 00:03:08.410
A sugar cookie almond milk latte, iced.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.260
I think everything settled to the bottom.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:12.620
Nope, yeah, that's OK.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:13.950
Chestnut pralines latte.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.660
Does anyone know what a pralines is?

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.200
I don't.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.585
Well, whatever it is, it's good.

00:03:18.585 --> 00:03:20.880
Yo, Starbucks is on it this year.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.880
They did not have a peppermint mocha

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.520
at the Starbucks we
went to, unfortunately,

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:25.868
but that is also available.

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:29.530
Also at Starbucks you can
get the bean blends to go.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.065
We have the peppermint mocha blend,

00:03:32.065 --> 00:03:33.570
have the Christmas blend,

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:34.540
and the holiday blend.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.200
One holiday drink to
look out for in the UK

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.660
is the venti eggnog latte.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.150
One of these contains 476 calories

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.910
as well as a whopping
54 grams of added sugar.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.930
Please. In the US, we
have three holiday drinks

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:48.200
that have 60 grams or more of added sugar.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:51.790
The venti crème brûlée latte
rocks 60 grams of added sugar,

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.415
while the venti peppermint mocha

00:03:53.415 --> 00:03:55.506
has 68 grams of added sugar,

00:03:55.506 --> 00:03:58.610
and the venti toasted
white chocolate mocha

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:02.267
has 69 grams of sugar.

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.025
69!

00:04:04.025 --> 00:04:06.200
Careful, Santa can read your thoughts.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.370
That means at least two drinks
during the holiday season

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:13.610
make the fourth- and
fifth-most sugary drinks

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:15.080
on the Starbucks menu.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.800
Japanese Starbucks didn't tell me

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.160
how much sugar is in
these Christmas drinks,

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.580
but we do have a calorie count.

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:25.630
A venti gingerbread
latte has 488 calories,

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:30.130
and a venti crème brûlée
latte has 497 calories,

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:33.080
and tall toasted white
chocolate Frappuccino

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.380
is 403 calories.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.880
The most calories award

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.100
goes to the venti toasted
white chocolate mocha.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:43.642
It has 669 calories.

00:04:43.642 --> 00:04:45.283
What have you done?

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.500
Very good.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.333
What about the food?

00:04:50.333 --> 00:04:51.840
Well, in the UK, we have
a bunch of new items,

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.440
as well as some classic favorites.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.780
First up we have this one,
the Festive Feast panini.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.610
Next up is the 'Tis the
Season turkey sandwich.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.876
Two new additions include a

00:04:59.876 --> 00:05:01.560
chocolate and orange s'mores toastie

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:04.003
as well as a blue cheese
and chutney toastie.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:07.000
Our last two sandwiches are
a Toastie To Be Thankful For,

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:07.890
lots going on,

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:10.740
and then finally a Very
Merry Beyond Meat sandwich.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.040
Then we're on to some
of the baked options,

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.470
starting with my favorite, South Pole Sam.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:16.610
He's making a return.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:17.847
He was in the last episode.

00:05:17.847 --> 00:05:19.638
I love him. He's still my son.

00:05:19.638 --> 00:05:22.080
Look at him! He's adorable!
How could you eat this?

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.170
Come on, look at him.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.850
Not only is South Pole
Sam still on the menu,

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:26.560
but he's been really busy this year,

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.390
'cause he's come back with a girlfriend!

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.120
This is North Pole Nat.

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:32.673
Maybe supposed to be a polar bear.

00:05:32.673 --> 00:05:33.720
Not 100% sure.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.670
So not only is it kind
of a forbidden romance,

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:37.890
it's also a very
long-distance relationship

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:40.120
between South Pole Sam and North Pole Nat,

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:41.780
but their love is just that strong.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.120
It carries them through.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.290
And I for one really hope
it works out for them.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.270
In less adorable but
still very delicious news,

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.910
the Christmas tree brownie is
back at Starbucks in the UK.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:52.380
Another returning favorite
is the Cranmerry muffin.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.740
It's basically just a cranberry muffin

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.920
with I think some either icing
or custard in the middle.

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:58.030
It's pretty good.

00:05:58.030 --> 00:05:58.960
Then we have two new additions,

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.380
starting with the toffee
nut latte cupcake.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:03.070
This is a coffee-flavored cupcake

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:05.720
topped with some chopped
nuts and a chocolate star.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:08.610
And, finally, we have
a red velvet loaf cake.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.350
As the name suggests,
it's a red velvet loaf,

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:11.510
and then it's topped with some icing

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.580
as well as some very
festive-colored sprinkles.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:17.050
In Japan, we have several
sweet holiday options,

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:20.075
which are a cranberry bliss bar

00:06:20.075 --> 00:06:22.266
and a chocolate pound cake.

00:06:22.266 --> 00:06:25.600
They also have gingerbread
cookies and a stollen,

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:27.790
which are currently unavailable.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:29.520
So sad.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.686
A stollen is a classic holiday bread

00:06:31.686 --> 00:06:34.669
with red cranberries, green pistachios,

00:06:34.669 --> 00:06:37.210
white powdered sugar, raisins,

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:41.310
almonds, walnuts, orange
peels, and marzipan.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:44.410
And also you can get a holiday cheesecake,

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:47.650
baked cheese tart, and
a chocolate forest cake.

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:50.600
But online order only.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:51.960
It's a new era.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:55.060
It's not like grandma's cookies.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:57.930
Here in the US, get yourself
a reindeer cake pop,

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.022
this little guy right here.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:07.853
Turns out he's delicious.

00:07:07.853 --> 00:07:10.153
Snowman cookie.

00:07:10.153 --> 00:07:13.870
Personal favorite, cranberry bliss bar.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.778
Now, you can get a slice of the bar

00:07:15.778 --> 00:07:18.261
or the bar tray to go.

00:07:18.261 --> 00:07:22.240
And also this year they have
the sugarplum cheese Danish,

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:25.257
which the Starbucks we went to
did not have, unfortunately.

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:29.220
In the UK, our KFC exclusives

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.900
are mostly focused on the gravy.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:33.070
First up, we've got this
gravy burger box meal.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:36.020
This comes with a gravy burger,
a chicken tender to dip,

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:37.870
a side of fries, and a side of gravy.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:39.430
If you're wondering
what a gravy burger is,

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.827
it's basically a chicken sandwich

00:07:40.827 --> 00:07:43.010
with some cheese and some gravy mayo,

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:44.670
but then it's also got
this hash brown on top,

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:47.070
into which they've kind of
pressed a circular divot.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:49.350
The idea is that you pour
more gravy on top of it,

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.680
it kind of holds it in there,
so that when you bite into it,

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:53.060
you get a lot of gravy in your bite.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:54.498
So I've poured a small amount of gravy.

00:07:54.498 --> 00:07:56.690
As you can see, it's
holding it nicely in place.

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:58.340
But we're not here for
a small amount of gravy

00:07:58.340 --> 00:07:59.890
in "Food Wars."

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:01.523
Now, that is a gravy burger.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:07.900
If that's somehow not
enough gravy for you,

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:08.742
you can also get a range

00:08:08.742 --> 00:08:11.020
of gravy bucket meals from a UK KFC.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:12.840
Firstly, you can get a
double gravy bucket meal,

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:16.010
which contains six pieces
of chicken, a large drink,

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.030
four orders of gravy,
four orders of fries,

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:20.300
one order of popcorn chicken,

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:22.820
and then you can choose
between either eight hot wings

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:25.150
or six boneless chicken strips.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:27.390
If you don't want to choose
between the wings or the strips,

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:28.960
you can also upgrade to
a triple bucket meal,

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.780
which contains them both
for a reasonable price

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:32.770
of 23 pounds 99 pence.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:34.050
Also, I know that's only three orders

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:34.933
of gravy instead of four,

00:08:34.933 --> 00:08:37.350
but one of them exploded
in the delivery transit.

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:38.983
Now, we're guessing that the
bucket meals aren't designed

00:08:38.983 --> 00:08:41.660
to be eaten by one person, but
the box meal definitely is.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.270
One of these box meals
contains 1,075 calories,

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:47.060
which is 53.75% of your daily allowance.

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:50.210
There's also 107.8% of
your daily sodium in here.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.100
One culprit for the high
sodium might be the gravy.

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.970
According to KFC, one portion of the gravy

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:56.260
contains 480 milligrams of sodium,

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:59.170
which is around 20% of
the total meal's value.

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:02.520
KFC is very popular in
Japan around Christmastime.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:04.280
Ever since the '70s,

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:07.490
KFC has been a part of the
Christmas tradition in Japan

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:11.632
because of a popular KFC
marketing campaign called

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:16.060
or Kentucky for Christmas.

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:20.530
And now it's become so normal
to have KFC on Christmas.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.370
And also very small percentage

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.420
of Japanese people are Christians.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:28.710
So Christmas is just fun event
to spend with your family,

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:31.410
or if you're dating, you spend Christmas

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:34.230
with your boyfriend or girlfriend.

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:36.396
And now, even now,

00:09:36.396 --> 00:09:38.191
I'm still looking for the one

00:09:38.191 --> 00:09:40.766
who can enjoy Christmas with me.

00:09:40.766 --> 00:09:42.400
Message me.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:44.020
I'm on the nice list.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:47.040
Since KFC for Christmas is so popular,

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:50.650
KFC requires you to reserve
your Christmas specials

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:55.048
weeks in advance to be picked
up closer to Christmas.

00:09:55.048 --> 00:09:57.900
Unfortunately, at the
time of this recording,

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:01.140
the food isn't yet available.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:02.480
I wanted to try them.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:04.980
So, KFC offers party barrels,

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:07.960
which are either an
eight-piece original chicken

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.600
or a four-piece original chicken

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:12.770
with four chicken tenders.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:16.485
Both barrel meals include
a minced chicken lasagna,

00:10:16.485 --> 00:10:17.870
glaçage chocolate cake,

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:20.237
and seasonal buckets and plates.

00:10:20.237 --> 00:10:21.770
Wow!

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:24.780
And also you can get
roast chicken and gravy

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.660
and roasted garlic thighs

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:30.535
and chicken breast with cheese sauce

00:10:30.535 --> 00:10:31.776
and barbecue chicken.

00:10:31.776 --> 00:10:34.100
Oh, by the way, if you haven't watched

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:36.875
KFC episode USA versus Japan,

00:10:36.875 --> 00:10:40.250
you should definitely watch, watch, watch

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:41.991
after watching this video.

00:10:41.991 --> 00:10:44.720
Here in the US, KFC,
for a very limited time,

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:46.345
and it totally got past me,

00:10:46.345 --> 00:10:48.669
has a very slick, very cool

00:10:48.669 --> 00:10:52.280
Finger Lickin' Chicken
Mitten Bucket Hugger.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:53.870
Apparently you had to preorder one

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:56.480
by, like, before November 13.

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:59.030
Anyway, it's a knitted sweater, like,

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:02.710
I don't know, Koozie for your KFC bucket.

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:04.285
It has mittens sewn into it.

00:11:04.285 --> 00:11:05.243
It is hilarious.

00:11:05.243 --> 00:11:06.670
Couldn't get my hands on one,

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:08.587
but if we could have
someone in graphics go ahead

00:11:08.587 --> 00:11:10.981
and just put it on there for me.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:15.425
Yeah! That's what it looks like.

00:11:15.425 --> 00:11:16.560
Pretty cool, huh?

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:18.920
What is available in
much larger quantities

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:23.359
is this, the KFC festive-design
Christmas bucket.

00:11:23.359 --> 00:11:25.942
It even has a little top there.

00:11:25.942 --> 00:11:26.833
That fun?

00:11:28.209 --> 00:11:29.301
[crash]

00:11:31.923 --> 00:11:33.173
In the UK, McDonald's is featuring

00:11:33.173 --> 00:11:34.773
two sandwich options for Christmas,

00:11:34.773 --> 00:11:38.430
a festive stack and also a
festive crispy chicken sandwich.

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:40.610
In the UK, the festive stack
contains some beef patties,

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:42.653
some cheddar cheese, a white cheese sauce,

00:11:42.653 --> 00:11:45.000
some bacon, some lettuce,
as well as some red onions,

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.250
whereas the festive crispy
chicken is a crispy chicken patty

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:48.940
with some bacon, some cheddar cheese,

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:50.790
I think there's some sage
and onion mayo in there,

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.720
as well as some cranberry sauce.

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:54.400
McDonald's in the UK has one festive side,

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:55.970
and it's these cheese melt dippers.

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:57.860
These are little disks
of Camembert cheese,

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.253
which are then breaded and fried,

00:11:59.253 --> 00:12:01.370
and they look and smell
really good, I gotta say.

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.690
And they also come with
this tangy tomato sauce,

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:05.060
which also looks pretty good.

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:06.800
I think it's just kind
of like a fancy ketchup.

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:07.940
And we have two dessert options,

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:10.780
including a Celebrations
McFlurry and a festive pie.

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:11.860
I'll get into a little bit more detail

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:12.760
on Celebrations later,

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:14.670
but what it is, is a
selection box in the UK.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:16.370
It's all of the kind of Mars brand candy,

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:18.650
so it's things like
Snickers and Maltesers.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:20.522
And they put little bits
of them into a McFlurry,

00:12:20.522 --> 00:12:21.550
and it's pretty good.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.000
The festive pie is basically
the apple pie shell,

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.500
but instead of the apple filling,

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:28.190
it comes with a mincemeat
and custard filling.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:29.320
Now, for those of you who aren't versed

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:30.760
in stunning British cuisine,

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:32.240
mincemeat is not actually beef.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:33.073
Please don't freak out.

00:12:33.073 --> 00:12:34.370
We're not putting beef
and custard together.

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:35.370
That would be weird.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.062
Mincemeat in the festive context refers to

00:12:37.062 --> 00:12:38.857
a mixture of fruits, things like raisins,

00:12:38.857 --> 00:12:40.636
little pieces of apple,
and things like that,

00:12:40.636 --> 00:12:41.811
which are simmered down in some sugar

00:12:41.811 --> 00:12:43.880
to create a kind of sweet, fruity mixture

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:46.200
and then added to things
like this or mince pies.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.680
Then, finally, we have
two hot drink options.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:49.520
We have a choco fudge latte,

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:51.010
and our final seasonal McDonald's item

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:52.730
is this hot chocolate deluxe.

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:55.630
In the US, our McDonald's
only has one exclusive drink,

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:57.890
the peppermint mocha, which
unfortunately was not available

00:12:57.890 --> 00:12:59.817
when we went to that McDonald's to get it.

00:12:59.817 --> 00:13:03.840
What they did have, thankfully,
is this holiday pie.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:04.850
I don't know what's in it.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:06.807
Mystery pie about to be solved.

00:13:08.983 --> 00:13:10.740
It tastes exactly like a sugar cookie.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:11.750
Very disappointing.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.825
In the US and the UK

00:13:13.825 --> 00:13:16.075
from December 13 to Christmas Eve,

00:13:16.075 --> 00:13:17.350
McDonald's has partnered up

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:19.858
with the queen of Christmas music,

00:13:19.858 --> 00:13:21.667
that's right, Mariah Carey,

00:13:21.667 --> 00:13:23.308
for the Mariah menu.

00:13:23.308 --> 00:13:25.374
Check this out. See that?

00:13:25.374 --> 00:13:26.480
Starting on the 13th,

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:28.790
if you spend over $1
on the McDonald's app,

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:32.370
there will be an exclusive
free menu item you can have.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.070
It's nice. It's kind of like
a McDonald's Advent calendar.

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:37.310
It's a pretty good idea.

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:39.000
Japan McDonald's is offering

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.170
two exclusive nugget dipping sauces

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:43.690
from now until next year.

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:47.183
We've got lobster and tomato cream sauce.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:52.670
In a nutshell, this is so good.

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:55.261
It's got strong lobster flavor.

00:13:55.261 --> 00:13:56.852
10 out of 10.

00:13:56.852 --> 00:13:58.100
Thank you.

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.770
Let's try kokuuma steak sauce.

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:02.795
So, koku means richness,

00:14:02.795 --> 00:14:05.120
and uma is deliciousness.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:08.390
And this steak sauce is a
Japanese-style steak sauce

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:10.238
based on soy sauce.

00:14:17.619 --> 00:14:19.290
This is so good.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.398
I could eat rice with this.

00:14:21.398 --> 00:14:22.706
Like, forever.

00:14:22.706 --> 00:14:26.962
These new exclusive sauces,
Santa Claus love them.

00:14:30.093 --> 00:14:32.132
In the UK, Pizza Hut only
has one festive offering,

00:14:32.132 --> 00:14:35.260
and it's this one, the hog roast pizza.

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:37.300
This is topped with
pulled pork, red onion,

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:40.060
a sage and onion stuffing,
and an applesauce drizzle.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:41.560
I'm really intrigued by
the applesauce drizzle,

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.223
so I'm going to have to give this a try.

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:46.740
Honestly, I'm kind of impressed by this.

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.040
I thought the applesauce would ruin it,

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:50.440
'cause I don't normally want
sweet things on my pizza,

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:51.898
but, yeah, it kind of all works.

00:14:51.898 --> 00:14:53.730
Hog roast pizza. Does
what it says on the tin.

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:54.960
Our Pizza Hut in the US

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:59.230
is offering this very
festive triple treat box.

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:02.035
Now, what this is, is a box, obviously,

00:15:02.035 --> 00:15:04.545
with two medium one-topping pizzas,

00:15:04.545 --> 00:15:07.690
five breadsticks, and Cinnabon mini rolls.

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:10.370
A-plus for presentation with Pizza Hut.

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:12.265
Wait a second. What?

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:15.235
Aw!

00:15:15.235 --> 00:15:17.576
This is not what's on the website!

00:15:17.576 --> 00:15:20.450
There was a thing that had,
like, shelves and stuff!

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:22.595
Show what it looks like on the website.

00:15:22.595 --> 00:15:24.380
And this is just, like, three pizza boxes.

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:26.610
I am so mad that this is what they did.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:29.520
This is not at all what I
thought this was going to be.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:33.130
So everyone can see how
disappointing this is.

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:35.400
Oh, this looks all beat up and stuff.

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:38.050
The whole point was it was
supposed to be a fun box!

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:40.600
This isn't that fun! This is regular.

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:42.080
Bah humbug.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.662
We have a special deal based
on Pizza Hut's mascots,

00:15:45.662 --> 00:15:47.620
Kazu and Mook.

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:51.580
Kazu is one of the most
famous comedians in Japan,

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:52.538
and also,

00:15:52.538 --> 00:15:56.640
Mook is one of the most
famous characters in Japan.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.760
And recently they have been appointed

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:00.710
as Pizza Hut's ambassadors.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.771
And this Christmas, you can get

00:16:02.771 --> 00:16:07.192
Kazu and Mook's Blissful
Half and Half pizza.

00:16:07.192 --> 00:16:09.960
Ta-da!

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:12.310
One half is for Kazu's favorite,

00:16:12.310 --> 00:16:14.780
Camembert and mozzarella,

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:18.390
and another half is for Mook's favorite,

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:22.510
meat sauce, thick-sliced
Ibérico, and margherita.

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:26.070
And also you can get a family
side set with this pizza

00:16:26.070 --> 00:16:28.803
that includes a chicken combo set.

00:16:28.803 --> 00:16:30.636
Wow!

00:16:30.636 --> 00:16:31.727
Festive.

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.410
In the UK, Domino's has
one Christmas pizza,

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:37.740
and it's called The Festive One.

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:39.575
This one comes with
sage- and onion-marinated

00:16:39.575 --> 00:16:41.100
turkey breast, some bacon,

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.708
some sausage, and some onion.

00:16:42.708 --> 00:16:43.767
Let's try it out.

00:16:45.145 --> 00:16:46.675
A little bit dry maybe.

00:16:46.675 --> 00:16:47.940
Maybe Domino's can redeem themselves

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.640
with these After Eight cookies.

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:50.652
For those of you who don't know,

00:16:50.652 --> 00:16:52.950
After Eights are a chocolate
and mint combination

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:54.080
which are generally kind of eaten

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:55.090
at the end of dinner parties.

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:57.000
That was the marketing back in the day.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.860
Obviously we are filming
this before 8 p.m.,

00:16:58.860 --> 00:17:00.470
so it's not a strictly enforced rule.

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:01.495
Let's give these a try.

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:04.280
OK, yeah, these are actually really good.

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:05.800
It tastes exactly like
the After Eight filling,

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:07.083
as I guess I'd expect.

00:17:07.083 --> 00:17:09.930
And yeah, just a really good
dark chocolate and mint cookie.

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:13.270
Our Domino's offer the
Christmas premium quattro,

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:15.710
which is separated into four sections.

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:19.230
We have smoked chicken with basil sauce,

00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:21.280
charcoal roast beef,

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:23.713
Italian juicy roast pork,

00:17:23.713 --> 00:17:26.950
and shrimp and scallop with crab sauce.

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:31.070
For dessert, we've got a cool mille crepe.

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:32.998
This is what it looks like.

00:17:32.998 --> 00:17:35.260
Hm. It's actually a huge one.

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:38.552
Not only these, but also
Domino's will be offering

00:17:38.552 --> 00:17:40.800
premium roast chicken soon.

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:43.102
It's gonna be festive!

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:47.240
Subway in the UK is featuring something

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:49.600
called a Tiger Pig sandwich
for Christmas this year.

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:52.530
It's basically a giant pig
in a blanket in a roll.

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:53.818
So, a pig in a blanket in the UK

00:17:53.818 --> 00:17:55.330
is not the same as it is in the US.

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:58.180
In the UK, it is a
sausage wrapped in bacon.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:01.730
Whereas in the US, I think
it's, like, a hot dog in pastry.

00:18:01.730 --> 00:18:02.930
That is correct, Harry.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.540
In the US, our pigs in a blanket

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:08.892
are normally tiny hot dogs
wrapped in croissant dough.

00:18:08.892 --> 00:18:10.740
And they're usually hors d'oeuvres

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:13.990
or what picky kids eat
at holiday parties. So.

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:16.370
That looks real gross.

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:18.190
Another festive sandwich
filling from a UK Subway

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:19.381
is Brie cheese.

00:18:19.381 --> 00:18:20.381
And then finally we have a festive

00:18:20.381 --> 00:18:21.773
dessert option at UK Subways,

00:18:21.773 --> 00:18:23.440
which is a chocolate orange cookie.

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:25.330
Chocolate and orange are a
really popular combination

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:26.430
around Christmastime in the UK.

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:28.070
I'm not really sure
where it originated from,

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:30.140
but there's a brand called
Terry's Chocolate Orange,

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:32.860
who do these kind of balls
of chocolate and orange.

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:34.620
Those are super popular
around Christmastime.

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:35.840
I think this is Subway's attempt

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.323
to kind of get in on the act there.

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:41.590
Now, one Christmas
tradition we have in the UK

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:43.480
when it comes to sweets
are selection boxes.

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:45.600
These are little tubs
filled with small sweets,

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:47.130
usually all from one brand.

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:48.755
So, for example, you have Heroes,

00:18:48.755 --> 00:18:49.963
which are owned by Cadbury,

00:18:49.963 --> 00:18:52.260
or you have Celebrations,
which are owned by Mars.

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:53.940
I'm not sure where the
association between Christmas

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:55.560
and selection boxes started in the UK,

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:56.810
but I know it's been going on for years,

00:18:56.810 --> 00:18:58.870
because I think Quality
Street and Roses in particular

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:00.150
have been around for decades.

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:01.360
One last thing to check before I hand over

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:03.092
is the contents of the Quality Street tin.

00:19:03.092 --> 00:19:05.550
It's become quite a divisive
topic in the UK recently

00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:06.952
because people feel shortchanged

00:19:06.952 --> 00:19:09.070
when they don't get enough
of the good ones in there.

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:10.520
I think the good ones
are generally considered

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:13.350
to be, like, the purple ones,
maybe the green triangles.

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:14.183
So let's count them out

00:19:14.183 --> 00:19:15.216
and see how many we're actually getting.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:23.020
So, we got four green triangles,

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:24.890
five of the orange chocolate crunch,

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.923
six of the caramel sticks,

00:19:26.923 --> 00:19:28.228
six of the toffee pennies,

00:19:28.228 --> 00:19:30.011
seven of the orange creams,

00:19:30.011 --> 00:19:31.393
eight of the fudge,

00:19:31.393 --> 00:19:33.085
five of the purple ones,

00:19:33.085 --> 00:19:35.430
five of the milk choc blocks,

00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:36.938
eight of the caramel swirls,

00:19:36.938 --> 00:19:39.537
six of the coconut eclairs,

00:19:39.537 --> 00:19:41.560
and seven of the strawberry delights.

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:42.970
Make of that what you will.

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:46.480
In the US, just about every candy brand

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:48.680
has a Christmassy-themed candy flavor,

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:50.313
shape, and/or package.

00:19:50.313 --> 00:19:51.560
There are too many to name in this video,

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:53.410
so I just went ahead
with some of the hits.

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:57.820
We got a Reese's peanut butter snowman,

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:01.110
Reese's holiday lights.

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:02.547
How do we think this is?

00:20:02.547 --> 00:20:04.140
Do you think it's actually on a string?

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:05.664
It's not!

00:20:05.664 --> 00:20:06.747
What?

00:20:06.747 --> 00:20:07.749
What?!

00:20:07.749 --> 00:20:09.149
Correct me if I'm wrong,
but they're connected

00:20:09.149 --> 00:20:11.280
by a string like lights, right?

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:13.075
They just gave me these!

00:20:13.075 --> 00:20:15.083
They're just chocolate eggs! Thank you.

00:20:15.083 --> 00:20:17.880
Reese's, you are on the naughty list.

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:20.120
Reese's peanut butter trees.

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:22.010
This is kind of like a Rorschach test.

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:23.840
What do you see?

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:26.360
I bet nobody said tree.

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:29.990
This is sooner to be my parents
fighting than it is a tree,

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:31.490
as far as what I see in here.

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:34.920
Nutcracker shape. I mean,
everything's suspect now.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:36.850
OK, they actually did it.

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:38.283
Congrats, you got one right.

00:20:39.377 --> 00:20:41.010
They also have white trees.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:45.678
One exclusive is Reese's peanut
butter cups, peanut brittle.

00:20:45.678 --> 00:20:47.310
I just saw these at Target on the fly.

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:50.667
They got gingerbread cookie
KitKats here in the US.

00:20:50.667 --> 00:20:52.297
Oreos, Oreos, Oreos.

00:20:52.297 --> 00:20:55.901
You can get yourself a
white-fudge-covered Oreo.

00:20:55.901 --> 00:20:57.551
So I guess that's supposed to be snow.

00:20:57.551 --> 00:20:59.910
Gingerbread Oreos.

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:01.627
M&amp;M's, M&amp;M's, M&amp;M's.

00:21:01.627 --> 00:21:04.476
So, M&amp;M's has, this year
they're doing snowballs,

00:21:04.476 --> 00:21:08.490
which looks to be white
chocolate pretzel M&amp;M's.

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:11.270
Pretzel M&amp;M's are so good.

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:13.930
Before I had them, I was like, who cares?

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:15.070
They're so good.

00:21:15.070 --> 00:21:19.084
And this one is just a white
chocolate sugar cookie.

00:21:19.084 --> 00:21:20.267
Holy s---.

00:21:22.367 --> 00:21:23.516
I know it sounds stupid,

00:21:23.516 --> 00:21:25.007
but it tastes exactly like a sugar cookie.

00:21:25.007 --> 00:21:25.850
These are really good.

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:27.040
This caught me by surprise.

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:28.780
I'd never even heard of
this. I saw it at Target.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:30.332
I had to get it and show it to you guys.

00:21:30.332 --> 00:21:34.710
Sour Patch Kids Xtreme cookie chalet.

00:21:34.710 --> 00:21:36.490
Cookie house? No, sir.

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:38.380
Chalet. Look at this thing.

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:40.263
This is either delicious or terrible.

